    "terminal_reason": "completed",
    "result_text": "I've implemented `summarize_ticket` in `app/summary.py`. The existing tests pass (2 passed), but none of them exercise the new function. I tried a quick check with a fake chat model, but that command needed approval and didn't run, so I haven't run the function itself.\n\n```python\ndef summarize_ticket(chat: BaseChatModel, ticket: Ticket) -> str:\n    \"\"\"A one-line summary of `ticket`; generation stops at the first blank line.\"\"\"\n    messages = [(\"system\", SUMMARY_PROMPT), (\"human\", ticket_text(ticket))]\n    reply = chat.invoke(messages, stop=[\"\\n\\n\"])\n    return str(reply.text).strip()\n```\n\n- **One request:** a single `chat.invoke` call with two messages: a system message with `SUMMARY_PROMPT` and a user message with `ticket_text(ticket)`.\n- **Stop at the first blank line:** the stop sequence `\"\\n\\n\"` is passed with the call, so it works with any LangChain chat model.\n- **Plain string:** I read the reply's `.text` rather than `str(message.content)`, which `translate.py` uses. Some providers return the reply as a list of content blocks, and `str()` on that would give a list representation instead of the text. `.text` pulls out just the text in either case, and I strip the surrounding whitespace."
